<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nghệ An province</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Nghe An</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nghệ An is a province of north-central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>, stretching from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-china-sea">South China Sea</a> coast to the Lao border, with its capital at Vinh. Long a frontier region between Dai Viet and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/champa">Champa</a>, it was a base for resistance movements against Chinese and later French rule, and the Tay Son emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quang-trung">Quang Trung</a> planned a capital there. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ho-chi-minh">Ho Chi Minh</a> was born in the province in 1890.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nghe-an-province.jpg" alt="Nghệ An province" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bùi Thụy Đào Nguyên · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:B%C3%A3i_bi%E1%BB%83n_C%E1%BB%ADa_L%C3%B2..jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
